                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1712-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>Roswell Pro Audio Mini K47</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Mini K47 is a large-diaphragm condenser microphone that is unique due its capsule design, its component quality, and its origin.</p><p>As the microphone&#8217;s name states, the capsule is a 34mm K47 style, based on Neumann&#8217;s design. It is a true single-backplate capsule, with the characteristic K47 drilling pattern. The diaphragms are made of Dupont Teijan brand Mylar. The front diaphragm is metallized with gold. </p><p>The mic uses a linear, transformerless circuit based on the Schoeps design. It delivers relatively high sensitivity (18mV/Pa) and low self-noise (13dBA).</p><p>Early production runs of the Mini K47 used a 2SK30A JFET, which has relatively low input capacitance (CISS), which avoids the performance reduction (in sensitivity and signal-to-noise ratio) that is common to microphones employing the popular 2SK170 JFET. These mics used a polystyrene input coupling capacitor. Signal capacitors were genuine Wima parts, imported from Germany.</p><p>The mic&#8217;s internals were significantly upgraded in early 2021. The Hartley oscillator that creates polarization voltage for the capsule was replaced with a CMOS based implementation that has lower noise and is more stable. The audio circuit was revamped; 100% of the components were upgraded. </p><p>The input circuit was redesigned to omit the coupling capacitor. The JFET was upgraded to a vintage part that Roswell has not disclosed; these transistors are hand-selected to meet noise and distortion requirements. Signal capacitors are vintage European parts, hand-matched to better than 1%. Resistors are Vishay branded, 50ppm, 1% tolerance. </p><p>The body sleeve is made of heavy steel.</p><p>Each Mini K47 goes through a 7-point test/QC program, including a 24-hour burn-in, an acoustic frequency sweep, and tests for polarity, sensitivity, and noise. A serial numbered, signed QC card is included with each microphone.</p><p><a rel="shadowbox" href="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images//mic_extras/roswell/minik47-cutaway-mount.jpg"><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/roswell/minik47-cutaway-mount-sm.jpg" class="thumb shaft" alt="Mini K47 with Cutaway shockmount" width="140" /></a><br />Through the summer of 2017, the mic shipped with a swivel mount and an elastic shockmount. Beginning in September 2017, the microphone was upgraded in numerous ways:</p><ul><li>The microphone&#8217;s headroom was improved by several dB, to make it easier to use the mic on moderate to high SPL sources.</li><li>A more durable metallic black sparkle finish was introduced.</li><li>The shockmount was upgraded to the Cutaway&trade; mount from the higher-priced Delphos microphone.</li><li>The mic began shipping in an aluminum flight case.</li></ul><p>Sometime in 2018, the company began including a Roswell branded, custom made microfleece storage pouch / dust cover with every Mini K47.</p><p><br />The company also offers matched pairs of this mic; the match criteria is 0.3dB in sensitivity (measured at 1kHz), and 1.5dB in frequency response (50&ndash;15,000Hz).</p><blockquote><p><cite>Paul Vnuk, Recording Magazine</cite></p><p>The Mini K47 is an impressive debut for Roswell Pro Audio. It is not just one of the best entry-level mics money can buy, it is also one of those workhorse mics that will find use in a mic locker forever, regardless of whatever other microphones one owns.</p></blockquote><p><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/roswell/mini-k47-rating-professional-audio.png" class="thumb shaft" alt="Mini K47" width="150" />The Mini K47 was rated &#8220;Outstanding&#8221; by Professional Audio magazine for its price-to-value ratio. (The award predates the shockmount and case upgrades of late 2017.)</p><p><iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/Qnxo2vdM90k" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; encrypted-media" allowfullscreen></iframe><p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Roswell/Mini-K47">Roswell Pro Audio Mini-K47</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2014.</p>
